1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,120
A sheet of paper is a mat of plant

2
00:00:02,967 --> 00:00:05,883
fibres, mostly air, held together by water.

3
00:00:06,191 --> 00:00:08,249
To make it by hand, you soak and beat

4
00:00:08,107 --> 00:00:10,617
bark until the fibres come apart, then lift them

5
00:00:10,464 --> 00:00:12,162
from a vat on a fine screen.

6
00:00:12,458 --> 00:00:15,886
The fibre matters. Kozo, used for Japanese washi, is

7
00:00:15,732 --> 00:00:19,288
about ten millimetres long. Eucalyptus, in most copy paper,

8
00:00:19,122 --> 00:00:19,984
is under one.

9
00:00:20,292 --> 00:00:22,872
Paper began in China, earlier than the usual date

10
00:00:22,719 --> 00:00:25,032
of a hundred and five. Fragments survive from the

11
00:00:24,878 --> 00:00:26,924
first century before the common era.

12
00:00:27,221 --> 00:00:30,242
It reached Baghdad by seven ninety-four, Spain by ten

13
00:00:30,112 --> 00:00:33,516
fifty-six, and Fabriano in Italy, where watermarks began in

14
00:00:33,363 --> 00:00:34,468
twelve eighty-two.

15
00:00:34,741 --> 00:00:38,598
In nineteen-oh-one, about seventy thousand Japanese households made washi.

16
00:00:38,433 --> 00:00:41,001
By two thousand and nine, two hundred and ninety-five

17
00:00:40,848 --> 00:00:41,547
remained.

18
00:00:41,890 --> 00:00:44,667
Meanwhile the world makes more paper than ever: about

19
00:00:44,514 --> 00:00:46,153
four hundred million tonnes a year.

20
00:00:46,427 --> 00:00:48,786
Hold a sheet under low, raking light, and its

21
00:00:48,609 --> 00:00:51,619
surface appears: fine laid lines from the mould's wires,

22
00:00:51,442 --> 00:00:52,827
and heavier chain lines.

23
00:00:53,123 --> 00:00:55,947
Ink tells the rest. On unsized paper it blooms

24
00:00:55,782 --> 00:00:58,071
into a cloud. Sized with glue, it stays where

25
00:00:57,895 --> 00:00:58,873
the brush left it.

26
00:00:59,169 --> 00:01:01,691
On a screen, we rebuild that surface from noise:

27
00:01:01,642 --> 00:01:03,990
layers of it, lit from a low angle, until

28
00:01:03,848 --> 00:01:05,012
it reads as paper.

29
00:01:05,390 --> 00:01:07,772
Every sheet keeps a record of its fibre, its

30
00:01:07,642 --> 00:01:09,316
mould, and the hands that made it.

